Market Overview
Telecom power systems provide the electricity conversion, distribution, monitoring, and backup capabilities needed to keep telecommunications networks operating continuously. These systems support mobile base stations, central offices, enterprise network facilities, small cells, edge sites, and other communications infrastructure.

As telecom operators expand 5G coverage and add more radio equipment, power demand at individual sites is increasing. Operators need systems that can support higher loads without requiring extensive changes to existing shelters and cabinets. Efficient rectifiers, modular power shelves, intelligent controllers, and integrated battery systems are therefore becoming increasingly important.

Asia-Pacific is the largest regional market, supported by extensive mobile networks, ongoing 5G investment, and large telecom infrastructure deployments. Across other regions, network modernization and the need to reduce energy costs are encouraging investment in advanced power-management solutions.

